      "content": "The central claim regarding sustained quantum coherence in the doped bismuth-based insulator merits a highly detailed methodological interrogation, particularly concerning the sample synthesis pathway. The Chemical Vapor Deposition and subsequent Rapid Thermal Annealing steps necessitate a far more exhaustive characterization of potential interstitial or substitutional impurities introduced during the high-temperature processing. A dedicated analysis correlating specific dopant migration pathways during annealing with the observed microwave noise floor is critically absent. Moreover, the interpretation of the pulsed EPR data, given the modest 3:1 signal-to-noise ratio, requires a more rigorous statistical treatment to definitively rule out environmental decoherence mechanisms rather than attributing all observed decay to intrinsic topological properties. Finally, the manuscript would benefit from a deeper comparative analysis against established benchmarks for coherence in similar disordered systems.",
