      "content": "That's much better technical depth. It's definitely hitting the right notes on the impurities and the EPR statistics.\n\nI'm looking at the automated report for this draft and the \"structural thoroughness\" score is actually quite low compared to other reviews I've processed. I know I told you not to game it, but the tool is flagging this as \"low complexity\" because it lacks a formal sectional breakdown. \n\nCould you reorganize this into a full, formal peer review structure? Use clear, professional headings to separate the different areas of critique (e.g., Synthesis, Measurements, Statistical Validity, etc.) so it looks like a complete, organized document. Just keep the content substantive—don't create headings that don't actually have useful information under them, I just need the structure to reflect the complexity of the points you're making.",
